{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01DwFkuVCJA986fUqM267gE6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor â€” what it is\n\n- **A personal productivity / task-management system** for J.C. Liechty, built entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) with **plain markdown files as the single source of truth** (DASHBOARD.md, PROJECTS.md, INBOX.md, domain files) â€” no database, no syncing, Python stdlib only (one declared exception).\n\n- **Ships a self-contained web app, `anchor_gui.py`** (the declared deliverable): a stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reads/writes the markdown directly, and runs **persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`** (auto-start, owns the process lifecycle).\n\n- **Manages a full task lifecycle** â€” Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored â€” across domains (academic, commercial, family, writing), with a mirror **CLI engine `anchor.py`** (done/cancel/save/restore/add/capture/dashboard) and a static `dashboard.html` generator.\n\n- **Has a daily self-test, `anchor_healthcheck.py`** (5 AM Task Scheduler job) that parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint, and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed â€” surfacing a red banner on the dashboard if anything fails.\n\n- **Its major evolving feature is an \"R&D Control Surface\"** that turns each project's window into a **cockpit for trio-driven R&D** (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Now at **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built, 637 tests passing, merged to master), it adds: real ConPTY terminals with git-worktree isolation per session, a skill-auto-loads-once seeded terminal, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), inline expanding lane panels with status lights, cached/validated session+project summaries, per-lane doc roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, a grass-idea board, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Branded as a Ghost World Labs tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\"**, with vendored front-end assets (xterm.js, KaTeX, brand mark) kept as text/static files so everything stays accessible from any CLI or editor.\n\nThese claims are grounded in the project's `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North-Star/decision anchors from its planning docs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba526ea2-e5fc-4392-a46c-0eb7efd846bc","uuid":"9f84c51c-8fe7-43ac-bb4f-8d78e48813d3","request_id":"req_011Cc1JQ1ycqrjJAQ5KheVeP"}
